-- title:
--   Single-place idèle generating a decomposition group at a cyclic layer
-- statement:
--   Let $F/E$ be a Galois extension of number fields with cyclic (hence abelian) group $\mathrm{Gal}(F/E)$, and let $\mathfrak f$ be an ideal of $\mathcal O_E$ that is an admissible modulus for the degree $[F:E]$: $\mathfrak f \neq 0$, and for every finite place $v$ of $E$ at which the chosen prime `primeAbove E F v` has non-trivial inertia subgroup in $\mathrm{Gal}(F/E)$, the power $v^{\,\mathtt{admissibleExpOfDegree}\,E\,[F:E]\,v}$ divides $\mathfrak f$. Let $r$ be a homomorphism from the idèle group $(\mathbb A_E)^\times$ to $\mathrm{Gal}(F/E)$ such that: the principal idèles (the image of $E^\times$) lie in $\ker r$; $\ker r$ is exactly the subgroup generated by the principal idèles together with the image of the idèlic norm attached to the base-change map $\mathbb A_E \to \mathbb A_F$ of `genuineBaseChange`; $r$ is surjective; and for every idèle $u$ adjusted at $\mathfrak f$ relative to $1$ (at each $v \mid \mathfrak f$ the finite component $u_v$ has valuation $1$ and $|u_v - 1| \le \exp(-\mathrm{ord}_v(\mathfrak f))$, and for each real embedding $\tau$ of $E$ the corresponding archimedean real projection of $u$ is positive) one has $r(u) = \prod_v \mathrm{Frob}_v^{\,\mathrm{ord}_v(u)}$, the product over finite places of the arithmetic Frobenius `artinFrob E F v` raised to the exponent of $v$ in the finite part of $u$. Let $v$ be a finite place of $E$ and $w$ a finite place of $F$ lying under which $v$ sits, i.e. $w \cap \mathcal O_E = v$. Then there exist $a \in E^\times$ and an idèle $x$ of $E$ such that $x$ has trivial infinite part and trivial finite component at every finite place other than $v$, the $v$-component of $x$ is the image of $a$ under $E^\times \to (E_v)^\times$, $r(x)$ lies in the decomposition subgroup of $\mathrm{Gal}(F/E)$ at the valuation subring of $w$, and every element of that decomposition subgroup is an integer power of $r(x)$.
--
--   This is the local–global compatibility step for the idèlic Artin map at a cyclic layer: the decomposition group at $w$ is realised as the cyclic group generated by the image of a single-place idèle coming from a global element of $E^\times$. It is used in the determination of the images under $r$ of the subgroups of idèles supported at $v$ and of the unit idèles there as the decomposition and inertia subgroups at $w$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_M4aHerbrand_exists_forall_mem_zpowers_idelicArtinMap_single_of_isCyclic.lean

